{
  "_help": [
    "Editable Swahili/English lexicon. Restart the server (or call reload) after editing.",
    "All matching happens on NORMALISED text: lower-case, accents removed, leetspeak decoded (b4ng1 -> bangi),",
    "spaced/dotted letters joined (b.a.n.g.i -> bangi), repeated letters squeezed (baaangi -> bangi).",
    "strong  : one hit is enough to BLOCK.",
    "review  : one hit sends the listing to human REVIEW.",
    "weak    : ambiguous words. Alone they only add a small score; with a 'context' word or emoji from the",
    "review_with_context / weak_with_context: decision when a review/weak word appears together with a context word or emoji of the same category.",
    "          same category they count as 'weak_with_context' (BLOCK or REVIEW, set per category).",
    "weak_cancel: words that show an innocent meaning; a lone weak word is ignored when one is present (never cancels strong terms or weak+context).",
    "allow   : legitimate phrases that are removed before matching (protects 'unga wa sembe', 'glue gun' ...).",
    "emoji   : emoji that act as context for weak words (never block on their own).",
    "Single words >= fuzzy_min_length in 'strong' are also typo-matched (bastora -> bastola).",
    "Add a word to 'fuzzy_exclude' if a normal word is being typo-matched to slang."
